      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the sum of the roots of the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\), we start by solving the equation step by step.\n\nFirst, we take the square root of both sides of the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\):\n\\[\nx - 5 = \\pm 3\n\\]\nThis gives us two separate equations to solve:\n\\[\nx - 5 = 3 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x - 5 = -3\n\\]\n\nWe solve each equation separately:\n1. For \\(x - 5 = 3\\):\n\\[\nx = 3 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 8\n\\]\n\n2. For \\(x - 5 = -3\\):\n\\[\nx = -3 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 2\n\\]\n\nThe roots of the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) are \\(x = 8\\) and \\(x = 2\\). To find the sum of the roots, we add these solutions together:\n\\[\n8 + 2 = 10\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the roots is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
