    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the given equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) and find the sum of its roots, we will follow a step-by-step approach.\n\n1. **Rewrite the equation in standard form:**\n   \\[\n   (x - 5)^2 = 9\n   \\]\n\n2. **Take the square root of both sides:**\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{(x - 5)^2} = \\pm \\sqrt{9}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the square root on the right-hand side, we get:\n   \\[\n   x - 5 = \\pm 3\n   \\]\n   This gives us two separate equations to solve:\n   \\[\n   x - 5 = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x - 5 = -3\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve each equation separately:**\n   - For \\(x - 5 = 3\\):\n     \\[\n     x - 5 = 3 \\implies x = 3 + 5 \\implies x = 8\n     \\]\n   - For \\(x - 5 = -3\\):\n     \\[\n     x - 5 = -3 \\implies x = -3 + 5 \\implies x = 2\n     \\]\n\n4. **Identify the roots:**\n   The roots of the equation are \\(x = 8\\) and \\(x = 2\\).\n\n5. **Sum the roots:**\n   \\[\n   8 + 2 = 10\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the roots of the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
